WEBVTT

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.760
"March"

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.310
Goody two shoes Hirano.

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.730
Shut up!

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:29.690
They're doing a hair check today,
so go dye yours black, you two!

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.690
Especially you, Ogasawara!

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:35.070
Who do you think today's plans are for?

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.160
Come on, dude. I'm fine.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.160
Mine <i>is </i>black.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.490
Fine how?

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:42.830
Blue highlights definitely won't fly!

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.290
I'll just cover it.

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:46.040
That won't work!

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.130
Yeah, blue is pushing it.

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:48.960
Really?

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.420
They'll definitely say something
to you, too, Sasaki.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:55.840
And what're you gonna do
during entrance exams?

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.050
We'll probably have flunked by then.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.350
Entrance exams...

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.730
One more year till graduation...

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.980
I've already known Mya-chan
more than six months...

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:15.780
How long can I hold back?

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.240
"April"

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.470
Morning.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:38.510
Morning.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:43.060
We're second years now.
What class did you get? I'm B.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.810
I'm class B, too.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.180
But...

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:48.770
What is it?

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:50.440
Nothing.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.770
I guess he's not here yet.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:55.690
Oh, I spotted Sasaki-senpai
over the break.

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:56.860
Huh?

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.990
He's working at a bakery.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:00.620
Oh?

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:04.660
I just walked by the place, though.
I didn't actually talk to him.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.540
--Kinda surprising, huh?
--He works at a bakery?

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:12.540
There are aspects of Senpai I don't know.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:19.630
Because he adjusts to me and we
basically only ever talk about manga.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:23.180
He's a good listener,
and probably popular.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.430
I bet lots of people confess their feelings...

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:32.400
You got a cold?

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.650
I just choked a little.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.990
I haven't seen him since that day.

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:47.040
I don't know how I should act when I do.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:11.520
"Sasaki and Miyano"

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:27.010
"Episode 4: 'Limit'"

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:42.070
Due to the rain, the ground may be
quite slick. Please exercise caution.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.120
Morning, Mya-chan.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.330
Senpai.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.880
Good morning.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.050
You left early today.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:04.420
Yeah. On rainy days,
my normal time is crazy.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:06.930
So then this time is better?

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:08.600
Way better.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.680
And at this time, I get to see Mya-chan.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:22.980
This is the first time we've
seen each other this term.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:25.490
Y-Yes.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:27.740
What'd ya do over the break?

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.820
Um, nothing really.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:31.080
Oh.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.340
Mya-chan, there's a seat.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:49.180
You have seniority.

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:50.720
Okay.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.680
In that case, Mya-chan, wanna sit on top?

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.810
Don't be silly.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:59.440
Then I'll hold your bag for you.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.610
Go ahead.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.190
Thank you.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:07.990
Mya-chan, this is super heavy.
Whad'ya got in here?

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:11.240
Um, my P.E. jersey
and stuff... you know...

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:12.530
And manga, too?

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:15.660
Hey, Senpai! Don't go through my bag!

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:18.250
Is this one I borrowed before?

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.580
No?

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.170
Oh, it's a novel.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:28.550
A-A spin-off novel came out, so...

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.760
Senpai, don't read it!

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:32.430
Did you hear me?

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:35.850
Hey, come on!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:01.330
So then there's a situation
where the <i>seme </i>cries.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:02.750
--He's always strong in front of the <i>uke</i>,

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:03.960
--It's stuck. So cute.
--He's always strong in front of the <i>uke</i>,

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.880
--It's stuck. So cute.
--yet that's the only time
he shows his vulnerability.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:07.920
--What do I do? Leave it?
--yet that's the only time
he shows his vulnerability.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:10.510
I love that kind of contrast...

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:12.050
And that's what happened.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:13.140
That's crazy.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:14.430
Right?

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:19.100
--Mya-chan, there's a petal in your hair.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.640
--So I wanna buy that thing.
--Mya-chan, there's a petal in your hair.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.940
--What thing?
--Oh? Thanks.

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:24.190
--That thing. You know, uh...
--Oh? Thanks.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:26.360
No, I don't know.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.400
Oh, Mya-chan, I found you!

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.400
So this is your class.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:09.440
Senpai...

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.530
Here's what I borrowed before the break.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.820
I forgot to give it back this morning.

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.160
Oh, right.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:17.780
Thanks for lending it.

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:19.160
Are you free?

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:21.660
Oh, yes.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:24.870
Oh, yea, I wanted to ask you something.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.710
Who's the <i>uke </i>in this one?

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:27.540
Huh?

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:31.050
It didn't have those
kinds of scenes, so...

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:33.800
Senpai, who do <i>you </i>think it is?

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:40.220
Hmm. I seem to remember
you like black-haired <i>ukes</i>...

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:41.810
I'll say the one with black hair.

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:45.600
Hey, could you not determine it
using my preferences?

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:46.440
"Preference determination"

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:48.770
Did I get it wrong?

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:51.150
There is no wrong answer.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:53.780
The author didn't reveal it, so...

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:57.320
I also thought the black-haired
guy was the <i>uke</i>...

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:02.790
But I didn't decide that based on
hair color--I just like handsome <i>ukes</i>!

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:05.330
Oh, and that why Hirano's an <i>uke</i>?

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:09.290
Listen, you don't have to grasp
absolutely everything...

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:11.920
--I feel like Hirano is pretty tall.
That doesn't make him a <i>seme</i>?
--So, remember what I told you?

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:13.510
--I feel like Hirano is pretty tall.
That doesn't make him a <i>seme</i>?
--Oh, yeah, that. What happened?

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:17.090
--In BL, someone with Hirano's height
can absolutely be an <i>uke</i>, too.
--A lot, and in the end they broke up.

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:18.890
--In BL, someone with Hirano's height
can absolutely be an <i>uke</i>, too.
--For real?

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:19.890
--He never lasts long.

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:20.760
--Mya-chan!
--He never lasts long.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:21.890
Oh, sorry!

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:36.700
That startled me.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:39.240
Sorry. Are you okay?

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:42.490
Yeah.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:46.620
Mya-chan, is your wrist okay?
You didn't twist it?

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:48.830
No, I'm f--

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:55.380
...ine.

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:01.810
I like you.

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:07.100
Be careful with your hand.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:09.730
Okay...

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:13.940
Well, I need to head back.

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:15.650
Lend me another some time.

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:16.950
Okay.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:25.040
Why...

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:27.790
Why did I think about that just now?

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:47.520
I think I interacted with him
the same as before.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:48.890
But...

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:57.190
...his demeanor...

00:10:57.190 --> 00:11:00.820
So then he like-likes me after all?

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:03.370
But still,

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:06.910
I like <i>girls</i>, not guys.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.120
In middle school, I...

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:09.580
"Miyano in middle school"

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:09.580
In middle school, I...

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.960
"Miyano in middle school"

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.960
Miyano!

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:12.500
Wear girls' clothes for a bit.
You'd look great in them.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:16.000
"The girl he liked."
Wear girls' clothes for a bit.
You'd look great in them.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:16.880
I don't want to.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:21.090
You'd look great.
It'd make a lovely picture.

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:22.680
I'm not happy to hear that.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:25.350
"Shook"

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:29.270
It's strange...

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:32.900
I never paid it much mind.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:37.070
But with Senpai's tone,
the look in his eyes...

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:39.740
It's like it became real all at once...

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:40.490
"Beh"

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:51.080
Did he mean "Ya wanna find out?"
the same way?

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:53.750
I mean, that's what it meant,
but not really...

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:57.250
I thought that was definitely a joke.

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:59.510
Was it really?

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:05.680
I do feel <i>moe </i>from BL,

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:06.970
but I...

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:09.390
"Tomorrow I'll Hold His Hand for Sure"

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.640
Regardless of gender!

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:14.850
I fell in love with you as a person!

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:16.560
Recognize that, dummy!

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:22.900
C-Calm down. Calm down.

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:24.450
Senpai is a guy.

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:27.330
I don't find him cute or anything else!

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:30.540
Oh, so that's why you were curled up?

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:33.710
Wait, what?

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:36.080
No, he's not really cute...

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:39.550
I think Senpai classifies as cool...

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:42.840
And anyway, I'm a guy, too.

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:43.800
Hold up!

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:46.890
Huh? With my frame,
wouldn't I be the <i>uke</i>?

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:51.270
No, no, no. There's quite a demand
in the world for short <i>semes</i>!

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:56.150
In fact, in some cases,
a short <i>seme </i>is standard!

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:04.570
Senpai.

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:10.040
Miyano?

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:11.750
That's not how I feel!

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:13.660
It's not like that!

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:16.040
Why do I immediately turn things into BL?

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:17.630
I'm sorry, Senpai!

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:28.090
"Several hours earlier"

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:29.220
"Several hours earlier"

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:29.220
Hirano, Sasaki says he left early.

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:31.640
Hirano, Sasaki says he left early.

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:33.310
What? How come?

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:35.310
Did he feel sick?

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:38.520
Dunno. He just said,
"It's too much. Going home."

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:40.690
What was too much?

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:57.370
Being that close is too much.

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:22.940
I'll go grab it.

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:24.900
The wind is strong this time of year.

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:27.320
But the breeze feels so nice.

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:29.740
Tashiro, you'll get the worksheets dirty.

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:31.620
Oop. Safe!

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:33.990
Kuresawa, warn me sooner!

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:37.040
I'm not your legal guardian.

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:37.870
Big bro!

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:40.000
You're older than me.

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:46.720
I guess it's around here.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:50.430
Like I said, it's not because
you're a <i>fujoshi</i>--

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:51.720
Hey!

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:55.060
She hung up.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:14:59.020
The <i>fudanshi</i>!

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:02.900
My name is Miyano, Ogasawara-senpai.

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:05.280
How come you're way over here?

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:08.240
A worksheet blew away.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:09.860
Oh, this.

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:15.790
Thank you.

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:20.790
I thought he was a scary guy,
but he's actually easy to talk to.

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:21.920
Senpai,

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:23.460
was that your girlfriend on the--

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:25.460
"Shook"

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:25.460
was that your girlfriend on the--

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:27.460
"Shook"

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:27.460
Um, I'm sorry.

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:29.050
"Shook"

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:29.050
Stepped on a landmine.

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:33.640
Me and my girlfriend are fighting.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:35.220
I see.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:37.970
We've been fighting for two months.

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:39.730
That's a long time.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:44.110
I went to her house the
other day to make up with her.

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:47.650
But when I went inside,
I heard her on the phone.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:51.700
I heard her shout,
"Nothing beats a delinquent <i>uke</i>!"

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:54.870
I went home without seeing her,

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:57.990
and so the fight continued...

00:15:57.990 --> 00:16:01.540
She's the type that gets loud
when she's excited.

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:03.580
So, you're a <i>fudanshi</i>, right?

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:04.210
Huh?

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:05.920
"Stare"

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:05.920
Huh?

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.090
"Stare"

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.090
Uh... yes...

00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:10.670
Listen, I got somethin' to ask ya.

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:11.760
Oh?

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:14.340
Do I seem like an <i>uke </i>to you?

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:15.890
Excuse me?

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:17.890
I ain't tryna be an <i>uke</i>, got it?

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.770
I-I know.

00:16:21.270 --> 00:16:25.060
See, if my girl sees me as an <i>uke</i>,

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:28.440
then I wanna play myself up
as her boyfriend.

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:32.360
But if I don't know what's
making me seem like an <i>uke</i>,

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:34.990
then that won't change anything.

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:36.530
I see...

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:40.450
So to avoid triggering
her <i>moe </i>points or whatever,

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:43.290
I read every manga she's got.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:46.630
But I found one about a...
slime? And a delinquent.

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:50.010
And now I just have no idea
what to do anymore.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:53.050
I can't understand what she wants.

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:57.970
I could say this about her manga, too,
but what on earth, man?

00:16:57.970 --> 00:16:59.760
Um...

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:04.020
I can't really comment about
the manga your girlfriend is reading,

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:06.520
but if she is going out with you,

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:10.440
then I think she actually likes you.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:12.440
Though she also likes BL,

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:15.450
that's a separate thing, you could say.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:19.410
I think you just happen
to be close to her favorite genre,

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:23.410
and she likes you as her boyfriend.

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:25.370
O-Oh.

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:30.750
Some people don't separate the two,
but I won't mention that.

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:34.590
Is that how it is for you?

00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:35.430
Huh?

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:39.800
You said you'd never treated
Sasaki as BL material.

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:43.220
You don't do that because
he's your boyfriend?

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:47.480
Y-You're mistaken.
We aren't in a relationship.

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:51.020
I thought you also liked guys.

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:55.030
You're mistaken.

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:04.950
Not that it matters either way.
And it ain't my business.

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:09.000
But what you said was helpful.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:12.840
If we make up, I'll introduce her to you.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:18.970
Senpai, how tall are you?

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:22.140
--Huh? That's Mya-chan's voice.
--Six feet.

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:25.180
In freshman year, I wasn't even 5' 7.

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:29.020
But I hit 5' 11'' in second year,
so there's hope for you.

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:30.270
Really?

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:33.150
--I dunno about genes though.
--He's talking with someone?

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:35.780
You're at perfect head-pat height.

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:38.240
What?

00:18:54.090 --> 00:18:56.590
Oh, it's you, Ogasawara. What's up?

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:58.880
Wh-Wh-What's up with you is the question!

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:00.470
Sorry, Mya-chan.

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:01.760
I-It's okay.

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:04.060
I totally freaked out.

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:04.890
My bad. My bad.

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:09.690
My heart almost leapt out of my throat.

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:13.400
I was getting advice
since I don't get <i>fujoshi</i>.

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:16.690
Yeah, your girlfriend.
You two gonna make up?

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:19.740
She asked to meet today, so we'll talk.

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:22.240
I see. Well, good luck.

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:23.990
Thanks.

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:26.200
Miyano!

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:27.830
I better head back.

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:34.040
Um... I hope things go well
with your girlfriend.

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:36.380
Bye.

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:38.210
Yeah, thanks.

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:40.510
Bye-bye.

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:43.180
Pretty blatant, don't ya think?

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:45.260
I'm heading back, too.

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:46.390
Okay.

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:05.620
I thought you also liked guys.

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:10.080
Even though I look at it in manga,

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:12.080
I don't at all.

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:14.790
I...

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:22.510
In middle school, I had a crush on a girl.

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:24.550
So I know I don't.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:30.680
I don't, but...

00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:36.150
When I think about Sasaki-senpai,
my chest feels tight.

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:38.230
Even though I don't think I do...

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:43.990
Could it be that I do like guys?

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:53.710
Does Sasaki-senpai?

00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:59.710
I suddenly...

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:01.630
...feel uneasy.

00:21:05.890 --> 00:21:07.850
Thanks for doing the trash.

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:09.310
Sure...

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:20.030
I couldn't fight it...

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:25.200
It won't stop...

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:30.990
You startled me.

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:32.120
What's wrong?

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:34.870
Nothing.

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:36.790
What's the next class?

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:38.380
Math III.

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:46.050
What am I gonna do?

00:23:18.270 --> 00:23:20.520
"The next day"

00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:24.400
You're fighting again?
What is it this time?

00:23:24.400 --> 00:23:29.110
You figured out she doesn't see you as BL.

00:23:29.110 --> 00:23:31.070
My favorite manga.

00:23:31.070 --> 00:23:33.530
She was turning it into BL!

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:37.330
Oh...

00:23:37.330 --> 00:23:39.540
Can I go now?

00:23:39.540 --> 00:23:41.170
I'll come with you.

00:23:42.750 --> 00:23:44.540
A fan work...

00:23:45.460 --> 00:23:47.760
"Episode 5: 'Bit by Bit'"
